# SAMPLE of chord_theory_graph_v0.4.ttl.gz: a few entries for viewing online. The full graph is the .ttl.gz file in this folder.
# Shown: Chords I, IV, V, vi, ii and iii with their relations to each other; transitions V>I, IV>I, ii>I and iii>I with their chords and cadential-variant links among them.
# 43 of 7025 triples; every triple here also appears in the full dump.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix wsim: <https://wsim.semanticaudio.net/ontology/wsim-0.1.ttl#> .

<https://wsim.semanticaudio.net/similarity/chord/IV-to-I> a wsim:ChordTransition ;
    rdfs:label "IV>I" ;
    wsim:cadentialVariantOf <https://wsim.semanticaudio.net/similarity/chord/ii-to-I> ;
    wsim:involvesChord <https://wsim.semanticaudio.net/similarity/chord/I>,
        <https://wsim.semanticaudio.net/similarity/chord/IV> .

